Lab: Create Organizational Units in Active Directory

Objective

Create new Organizational Units in Active Directory on a new Hyper-V server. The Structure will mirror the company's departments.

Environment

Tools Used

Windows Server 2019 Datacenter
Virtual Machines (VM)

Operating System

Windows Server 2019 Datacenter

Skills Practiced

Active Directory Administration
Organizational Unit (OU) Management
Directory Structure Management
Active Directory Organization
Administrative Configuration

Actions Performed

1. Upon logging in, I opened Hyper-V Manager and located the correct Virtual Machine running the required server. I connected to that VM. 
2. After connecting, the Server Manager is populated. I opened the Tools menu and clicked on Active Directory Users and Computers. This would allow me to create the Organizational Units.
3. Using the domain tree, I expanded the domain structure to view the available Organizational Units (OUs) and containers. 
4. Verified the requested Organizational Units did not already exist. Opened the New Object – Organizational Unit menu by right-clicking the domain tree.
5. Verified the new OU would be created in the correct location. I entered the department name into the Organizational Unit name field.
6. After verifying the OU name and location, I clicked OK to create the Organizational Unit.
7. Upon clicking OK, the new Organizational Unit appeared within the domain tree.
8. This process was repeated for seven additional Organizational Units.
9. The Sales department required two additional sub-OUs. I opened the parent Sales OU and repeated the process to create the required sub-OUs.
10. Verified each Organizational Unit was created within the correct domain structure and location. Verified all OU names matched the required department names and confirmed the Sales sub-OUs were created under the appropriate parent OU.
11. Documented findings and ended lab

